 # Working notes: 70c9dccdcc4d
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Review d21992d34c6ba325
+
+The imported 1.2.0 sampler used raw RNG for all declared axes, so exact overrides
+were not authoritative or observable and unknown keys were accepted. It also
+sampled only radius-bounded color-8 cells even though the canonical demonstrations
+are equally explained by the stronger shortcut “transpose every 8,” making the
+radius condition unteachable.
+
+Version 2.0.0 routes all six declared axes through keyed `GenCtx` draws, rejects
+unknown/non-integer exact overrides, and uses constructive 10x14 templates that
+cover all 64 source/target orientation pairs at the minimum dimensions. Ordinary
+draws include 1..4 exterior distractors plus a non-symmetric near motif; exact
+callers may request zero distractors. The canonical Racket authority and rule hash
+`06513d532f1c` were not changed.
+
+Task-local tests and the independent geometry probe live under `tests/` and
+`workspace/`. The before/after evidence, exact shortcut witness, larger lesson
+census, solve records, and adversarial audits are retained under the packet-level
+`checks/`, `solve/`, and `solve-blind/` directories. No prior associated review
+record was present in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`; the imported source and
+canonical examples were the only starting leads.
